    "https://www.mun.ca/hr/careers/": {
      "title": "Human Resources|People and Culture",
      "description": "Careers | Human Resources | Memorial University of\n Newfoundland Search: Search A-Z Directory Admissions Calendar Campus Maps Careers Faculties and Schools International Libraries People and Departments About Become A Student Campuses Give to Memorial Programs Research Alumni Faculty & Staff Students Visitors my.mun.ca Brightspace Student Self-Service Employee Self-Service Email Other MUN Login Services Memorial University Jump to A-Z Directory Admissions Calendar Campus Maps Careers Faculties\n and\n Schools International Libraries People and\n Departments Log in my.mun.ca Brightspace Student Self-Service Employee Self-Service Email Other MUN Login Services Alumni Faculty & Staff Students Visitors Human Resources | People and Culture Login About Us Mission, Vision, Values and Principles Contact Us Hours of Operation MyHR My Employment Conflict of Interest Employee Self Service Employee Guides Salary Scales Collective Agreements Holiday Schedule Leave Life Events CUPE Maternity/Parental/Adoption Leave Retirement Planning Flexible Work Arrangements Severance and Other Post Employment Benefits Exit Management New Employees Employee Orientation Things You May Need to Know Work Hours New Faculty Information Employment Benefits Pension Group Insurance Home, auto and travel insurance Leave Life Events Funding and Reimbursement Programs Specialty Select Payroll and Tax Information Payroll Information Tax Information Salary Scales Employment Equity Recruiting for Diversity Self Identification Accomodations Joint Equity Committee Resources Employee Development Academic Credit Courses SkillsBuild CUPE PD Fund Health and Safety Training Employee Well-being Respectful Workplace Employee Assistance Program Wellness Programs Psychological Health and Safety Ergonomics Program Injury and Accident Reporting Awards and Recognition President's Awards for Exemplary Employees President's Award Exceptional Community Service Service Awards Job Evaluation When Job Evaluation Should Occur What Job Evaluation Is and Is Not Job Evaluation Process Job Evaluation Appeal Process Hiring and Managing Policies, Procedures, and Guidelines Careers Retirees Notices Life Events MUNPA Administrators Hiring and Managing On-Boarding Guide Checklists Respectful Workplace Compensation Leave CUPE Maternity/Parental/Adoption Leave Exit Management Recognizing Retirement Collective Agreements Job Design and Evaluation Position Control Virtual Interview Tips Student and Other Positions Temporary Staffing Labrador Benefits Agreement OnBase Banner HR Policies, Procedures and Guidelines Human Resources Policies Guidelines Policy Education and Resources Faculty Load and Compensation Payroll and Leave Entry Deadlines Payroll Report Job Aids (Finance) Human Resources Forms Job Specifications Human Resources | People and Culture Home Careers Careers Find a position that is right for you and apply today. For information on applying for non-academic positions, please visit how to apply . There are also opportunities for students and Postdoctoral Fellows. Student employment programs include MUCEP , ISWEP , GradSWEP and SWASP and some schools and faculties offer experiential learning opportunities through co-operative education . Student employment rates are available here . Postdoctoral Fellows play an integral role in the teaching and research undertaken at Memorial University. Positions for Postdoctoral Fellows are regularly posted here . Working at Memorial Please note: available benefits can vary based on the role, employment type and campus. Make Your Mark At Memorial University, we nurture a culture where incredible people can use their talents and creativity to empower our students and build a better tomorrow. If you’re ready for a career where work and life really click, and where you can make a positive difference, then find your place with us. Newfoundland and Labrador's University Facebook Instagram Youtube Linked Tiktok We acknowledge that the lands on which Memorial\n University's campuses are situated are in the traditional\n territories of diverse Indigenous groups, and\n we acknowledge with respect the diverse histories\n and cultures of the Beothuk, Mi'kmaq, Innu, and\n Inuit of this province. A-Z Directory Accessibility Careers Contact Emergency Privacy Web Feedback Site\n Map | Last Updated: May 13, 2026 Copyright @2026 Memorial University of Newfoundland. Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada."
    },
    "https://mun.ca/academic-careers/": {
      "title": "Academic Careers",
      "description": "Academic Careers | Academic Careers | Memorial University of\n Newfoundland Search: Search A-Z Directory Admissions Calendar Campus Maps Careers Faculties and Schools International Libraries People and Departments About Become A Student Campuses Give to Memorial Programs Research Alumni Faculty & Staff Students Visitors my.mun.ca Brightspace Student Self-Service Employee Self-Service Email Other MUN Login Services Memorial University Jump to A-Z Directory Admissions Calendar Campus Maps Careers Faculties\n and\n Schools International Libraries People and\n Departments Log in my.mun.ca Brightspace Student Self-Service Employee Self-Service Email Other MUN Login Services Alumni Faculty & Staff Students Visitors Academic Careers Login Opportunities Faculty of Business Administration Faculty of Education Faculty of Engineering and Applied Science Faculty of Humanities & Social Sciences Faculty of Nursing Faculty of Science School of Arctic and Subarctic Studies School of Human Kinetics and Recreation School of Music School of Social Work Memorial University Libraries Office of the Provost and VP (Academic) Office of the President Academic Careers Academic Careers Memorial’s greatest strength is its people, working together across our province, our world and for our futures. We are Team Memorial. Faculty members at Memorial are part of a diverse community engaged in teaching, research, public engagement and collaboration across Newfoundland and Labrador and beyond. Learn more about specific academic job postings in the Opportunities section. Memorial University is committed to employment equity and diversity and encourages applications from all qualified candidates, including women; people of any sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression; Indigenous peoples; visible minorities, and racialized people; and people with disabilities.  As part of Memorial University's commitment to employment equity, all applicants are invited to identify themselves as a member of a target group(s) as appropriate.  Applicants cannot be considered as a member of a target group(s) unless they complete an employment equity survey.  If you do not receive a survey or have any questions, please contact equity@mun.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadian Citizens and Permanent Residents will be given priority. Newfoundland and Labrador's University Facebook Instagram Youtube Linked Tiktok We acknowledge that the lands on which Memorial\n University's campuses are situated are in the traditional\n territories of diverse Indigenous groups, and\n we acknowledge with respect the diverse histories\n and cultures of the Beothuk, Mi'kmaq, Innu, and\n Inuit of this province. A-Z Directory Accessibility Careers Contact Emergency Privacy Web Feedback Site\n Map | Last Updated: Aug 10, 2023 Copyright @2026 Memorial University of Newfoundland. Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada."
    },
